# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# KARAHOCA env templates have been split by service.
#
# Production (Coolify — two services):
#   - karahoca-api  → use .env.api.example  (Runtime variables)
#   - karahoca-web  → use .env.web.example  (Build Time variables, VITE_*)
#
# Local development (single machine running both stacks via `npm run dev`):
#
#     # Bash / WSL:
#     cat .env.api.example .env.web.example > .env
#
#     # PowerShell:
#     Get-Content .env.api.example, .env.web.example | Set-Content .env
#
# Then open .env and fill in the secrets that ship empty (JWT_SECRET,
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY, ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH, etc.). For local dev you'll
# usually also flip:
#
#     VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:5000
#     ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
#     SITE_URL=http://localhost:5173
#     FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:5173
#
# server-bootstrap.mjs and Vite both read .env at the project root, so a
# single combined file is enough for the local two-process setup.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
